IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap1-logic`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2014(a), (b), (c): who may participate, the uniform standards, and the income standards.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text; nothing here is "verified against the official text").
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE is the text's no in its own words (the branch quotes them);
-- NOTHING is "not covered" (the branch says why). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seams taken as INPUTS: s 2012(j) (household includes an elderly or disabled member), s 2012(m)(4), s 2015(b), (d)(2), (g), (r), s 2015, s 2025(e)(1).
-- The FY 2027 income standards are the USDA's figures (inputs/fna-snap-cola-fy2027.txt), not the Act's words; the Act sets them as a poverty line.

§ `s 2014(a) Income and other financial resources as substantial limiting factors`

-- src:215 | Participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be limited to those households whose incomes and other financial resources, held singly or in joint ownership, are determined to be a substantial limiting factor in permitting them to obtain a more nutritious diet.
@ref s 2014(a), first sentence (src:215)
GIVEN `the household's incomes and other financial resources are determined to be a substantial limiting factor in permitting it to obtain a more nutritious diet` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(a) the household may participate in the program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the household's incomes and other financial resources are determined to be a substantial limiting factor in permitting it to obtain a more nutritious diet`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be limited to those households"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a limit names who is outside; it does not say that everyone inside may participate

-- A member's receipt of a benefit listed in the second sentence: a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act,
-- supplemental security income under title XVI, or aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, X, XIV or XVI.
DECLARE `s 2014(a) member` HAS
    `receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `receives aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:215 | Notwithstanding any other provisions of this chapter except subsections (b), (d)(2), (g), and (r) of section 2015 of this title and section 2012(m)(4) of this title, households in which each member receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.], or aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq., 1201 et seq., 1351 et seq., or 1381 et seq.], shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2014(a), second sentence (src:215)
GIVEN member IS A `s 2014(a) member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2014(a) the member receives one of the listed benefits` MEANS
        member's `receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act`
    OR  member's `receives supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act`
    OR  member's `receives aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act`

-- src:215 | Notwithstanding any other provisions of this chapter except subsections (b), (d)(2), (g), and (r) of section 2015 of this title and section 2012(m)(4) of this title, households in which each member receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.], or aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq., 1201 et seq., 1351 et seq., or 1381 et seq.], shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2014(a), second sentence (src:215)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 2014(a) member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2014(a) each member of the household receives one of the listed benefits` MEANS
    (NOT (members EQUALS EMPTY)) AND all (GIVEN m YIELD `s 2014(a) the member receives one of the listed benefits` m) members

-- src:215 | Notwithstanding any other provisions of this chapter except subsections (b), (d)(2), (g), and (r) of section 2015 of this title and section 2012(m)(4) of this title, households in which each member receives benefits under a State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), supplemental security income benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.], or aid to the aged, blind, or disabled under title I, X, XIV, or XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 301 et seq., 1201 et seq., 1351 et seq., or 1381 et seq.], shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2014(a), second sentence (src:215)
GIVEN `each member of the household receives one of the listed benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(b) the exception in subsection (b) applies to the household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(d)(2) the exception in subsection (d)(2) applies to the household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(g) the exception in subsection (g) applies to the household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2015(r) the exception in subsection (r) applies to the household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(m)(4) the individual or group may constitute a household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(a) the household is eligible because each member receives a listed benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `each member of the household receives one of the listed benefits`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "households in which each member receives benefits" names the households the sentence reaches; it does not say what follows for the others
        IF  `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015(b) the exception in subsection (b) applies to the household`
            OR `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015(d)(2) the exception in subsection (d)(2) applies to the household`
            OR `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015(g) the exception in subsection (g) applies to the household`
            OR `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015(r) the exception in subsection (r) applies to the household`
            OR `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(m)(4) the individual or group may constitute a household`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notwithstanding any other provisions of this chapter except subsections (b), (d)(2), (g), and (r) of section 2015 of this title and section 2012(m)(4) of this title" (the sentence does not override an excepted provision that applies; "except", marginal reading (a))
        IF  `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(b) the exception in subsection (b) applies to the household`
            AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(d)(2) the exception in subsection (d)(2) applies to the household`
            AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(g) the exception in subsection (g) applies to the household`
            AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015(r) the exception in subsection (r) applies to the household`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "households in which each member receives benefits ... shall be eligible to participate"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an exception's answer was not supplied

-- src:215 | Except for sections 2015, 2025(e)(1), and section 2012(m)(4) of this title, households in which each member receives benefits under a State or local general assistance program that complies with standards established by the Secretary for ensuring that the program is based on income criteria comparable to or more restrictive than those under subsection (c)(2), and not limited to one-time emergency payments that cannot be provided for more than one consecutive month, shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2014(a), third sentence (src:215)
GIVEN `each member of the household receives benefits under a State or local general assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program complies with the Secretary's standards for ensuring that it is based on income criteria comparable to or more restrictive than those under subsection (c)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the program is not limited to one-time emergency payments that cannot be provided for more than one consecutive month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2015 a provision of section 2015 applies to the household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2025(e)(1) section 2025(e)(1) applies to the household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(m)(4) the individual or group may constitute a household` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(a) the household is eligible because each member receives general assistance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF  (NOT `each member of the household receives benefits under a State or local general assistance program`)
            OR (NOT `the program complies with the Secretary's standards for ensuring that it is based on income criteria comparable to or more restrictive than those under subsection (c)(2)`)
            OR (NOT `the program is not limited to one-time emergency payments that cannot be provided for more than one consecutive month`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence reaches only households whose members all receive general assistance of the kind it describes
        IF  `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2015 a provision of section 2015 applies to the household`
            OR `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2025(e)(1) section 2025(e)(1) applies to the household`
            OR `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(m)(4) the individual or group may constitute a household`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except for sections 2015, 2025(e)(1), and section 2012(m)(4) of this title, households in which each member receives benefits ... shall be eligible" (an excepted provision that applies takes the household out of the sentence; "except", marginal reading (a))
        IF  `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2015 a provision of section 2015 applies to the household`
            AND `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2025(e)(1) section 2025(e)(1) applies to the household`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "households in which each member receives benefits under a State or local general assistance program ... shall be eligible"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of an excepted provision was not supplied

-- src:215 | Assistance under this program shall be furnished to all eligible households who make application for such participation.
@ref s 2014(a), fourth sentence (src:215)
GIVEN `the household is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household has made application for participation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(a) assistance must be furnished to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is eligible` AND `the household has made application for participation`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be furnished to all eligible households who make application"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is owed "to all eligible households who make application"; the text is silent on anyone else

§ `s 2014(b) Eligibility standards`

-- src:217 | Except as otherwise provided in this chapter, the Secretary shall establish uniform national standards of eligibility (other than the income standards for Alaska, Hawaii, Guam, and the Virgin Islands of the United States established in accordance with subsections (c) and (e) of this section) for participation by households in the supplemental nutrition assistance program in accordance with the provisions of this section.
@ref s 2014(b), first sentence (src:217)
GIVEN `the standard is an income standard for Alaska, Hawaii, Guam, or the Virgin Islands of the United States established in accordance with subsections (c) and (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this chapter otherwise provides for the difference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(b) a standard of eligibility may differ from place to place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the standard is an income standard for Alaska, Hawaii, Guam, or the Virgin Islands of the United States established in accordance with subsections (c) and (e)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "(other than the income standards for Alaska, Hawaii, Guam, and the Virgin Islands of the United States established in accordance with subsections (c) and (e) of this section)"
        IF `this chapter otherwise provides for the difference`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except as otherwise provided in this chapter" points to provisions outside this row
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall establish uniform national standards of eligibility"

-- src:217 | No plan of operation submitted by a State agency shall be approved unless the standards of eligibility meet those established by the Secretary
@ref s 2014(b), second sentence (src:217)
GIVEN `the standards of eligibility in the plan meet those established by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(b) the plan of operation may be approved` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the standards of eligibility in the plan meet those established by the Secretary`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No plan of operation submitted by a State agency shall be approved unless the standards of eligibility meet those established by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" states a condition that must be met; it does not say that a plan meeting it is approved

-- src:217 | no State agency shall impose any other standards of eligibility as a condition for participating in the program.
@ref s 2014(b), second sentence (src:217)
GIVEN `the State agency imposes a standard of eligibility other than those established by the Secretary as a condition for participating in the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(b) the State agency may impose the standard` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency imposes a standard of eligibility other than those established by the Secretary as a condition for participating in the program`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no State agency shall impose any other standards of eligibility as a condition for participating in the program"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar reaches "any other standards of eligibility as a condition for participating"; the text is silent on anything else the agency imposes

§ `s 2014(c) Gross income standard`

-- FY 2027 DATA: the Act sets the standards as the poverty line (and 30 per centum above it); the figures below are the USDA's
-- cost-of-living page for fiscal year 2027 (1 October 2026 to 30 September 2027), copied by tools/gen_tables.py. They are INPUT DATA,
-- not statute: they change every 1 October, and a substitution would change every answer that reads them.
-- FY 2027 net monthly income limit, 100 percent of the poverty level (USDA Table 1). Source: lines 21-30 of inputs/fna-snap-cola-fy2027.txt (USDA's rounded figures, not the Act's words).
-- Columns, in the core's order: the 48 States and DC, Alaska urban, Alaska rural 1, Alaska rural 2, Guam, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands.
-- The USDA prints one Alaska column and one column for the 48 States, Guam and the Virgin Islands, so those figures are repeated.
`s 2014(c)(1) Table 1 net monthly income limit, FY 2027` MEANS `Annual table` WITH
    `fiscal year`    IS 2027
    `what it states` IS "FY 2027 net monthly income limit, 100 percent of the poverty level (USDA Table 1)"
    `the rows`       IS LIST
        (`Table row` OF 1, (`Dollars by area` OF 1330, 1663, 1663, 1663, 1330, 1530, 1330))
      , (`Table row` OF 2, (`Dollars by area` OF 1804, 2255, 2255, 2255, 1804, 2075, 1804))
      , (`Table row` OF 3, (`Dollars by area` OF 2277, 2846, 2846, 2846, 2277, 2619, 2277))
      , (`Table row` OF 4, (`Dollars by area` OF 2750, 3438, 3438, 3438, 2750, 3163, 2750))
      , (`Table row` OF 5, (`Dollars by area` OF 3224, 4030, 4030, 4030, 3224, 3707, 3224))
      , (`Table row` OF 6, (`Dollars by area` OF 3697, 4621, 4621, 4621, 3697, 4251, 3697))
      , (`Table row` OF 7, (`Dollars by area` OF 4170, 5213, 5213, 5213, 4170, 4795, 4170))
      , (`Table row` OF 8, (`Dollars by area` OF 4644, 5805, 5805, 5805, 4644, 5340, 4644))

-- Each additional member above 8: a dollar amount PER PERSON, not a total for a household of 9 (s 2014(c)(1) Table 1 net monthly income limit, FY 2027).
`s 2014(c)(1) Table 1 net monthly income limit, FY 2027, each additional member` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 474, 592, 592, 592, 474, 545, 474

-- FY 2027 gross monthly income limit, 130 percent of the poverty level (USDA Table 2). Source: lines 33-42 of inputs/fna-snap-cola-fy2027.txt (USDA's rounded figures, not the Act's words).
-- Columns, in the core's order: the 48 States and DC, Alaska urban, Alaska rural 1, Alaska rural 2, Guam, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands.
-- The USDA prints one Alaska column and one column for the 48 States, Guam and the Virgin Islands, so those figures are repeated.
`s 2014(c)(2) Table 2 gross monthly income limit, FY 2027` MEANS `Annual table` WITH
    `fiscal year`    IS 2027
    `what it states` IS "FY 2027 gross monthly income limit, 130 percent of the poverty level (USDA Table 2)"
    `the rows`       IS LIST
        (`Table row` OF 1, (`Dollars by area` OF 1729, 2162, 2162, 2162, 1729, 1989, 1729))
      , (`Table row` OF 2, (`Dollars by area` OF 2345, 2931, 2931, 2931, 2345, 2697, 2345))
      , (`Table row` OF 3, (`Dollars by area` OF 2960, 3700, 3700, 3700, 2960, 3404, 2960))
      , (`Table row` OF 4, (`Dollars by area` OF 3575, 4469, 4469, 4469, 3575, 4112, 3575))
      , (`Table row` OF 5, (`Dollars by area` OF 4191, 5238, 5238, 5238, 4191, 4819, 4191))
      , (`Table row` OF 6, (`Dollars by area` OF 4806, 6008, 6008, 6008, 4806, 5527, 4806))
      , (`Table row` OF 7, (`Dollars by area` OF 5421, 6777, 6777, 6777, 5421, 6234, 5421))
      , (`Table row` OF 8, (`Dollars by area` OF 6037, 7546, 7546, 7546, 6037, 6941, 6037))

-- Each additional member above 8: a dollar amount PER PERSON, not a total for a household of 9 (s 2014(c)(2) Table 2 gross monthly income limit, FY 2027).
`s 2014(c)(2) Table 2 gross monthly income limit, FY 2027, each additional member` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 616, 770, 770, 770, 616, 708, 616

-- FY 2027 gross monthly income limit where elderly or disabled members are a separate household, 165 percent (USDA Table 3). Source: lines 45-54 of inputs/fna-snap-cola-fy2027.txt (USDA's rounded figures, not the Act's words).
-- Columns, in the core's order: the 48 States and DC, Alaska urban, Alaska rural 1, Alaska rural 2, Guam, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands.
-- The USDA prints one Alaska column and one column for the 48 States, Guam and the Virgin Islands, so those figures are repeated.
`s 2014(c) Table 3 gross monthly income limit where elderly or disabled members are a separate household, FY 2027` MEANS `Annual table` WITH
    `fiscal year`    IS 2027
    `what it states` IS "FY 2027 gross monthly income limit where elderly or disabled members are a separate household, 165 percent (USDA Table 3)"
    `the rows`       IS LIST
        (`Table row` OF 1, (`Dollars by area` OF 2195, 2744, 2744, 2744, 2195, 2525, 2195))
      , (`Table row` OF 2, (`Dollars by area` OF 2976, 3720, 3720, 3720, 2976, 3423, 2976))
      , (`Table row` OF 3, (`Dollars by area` OF 3757, 4696, 4696, 4696, 3757, 4321, 3757))
      , (`Table row` OF 4, (`Dollars by area` OF 4538, 5672, 5672, 5672, 4538, 5219, 4538))
      , (`Table row` OF 5, (`Dollars by area` OF 5319, 6649, 6649, 6649, 5319, 6116, 5319))
      , (`Table row` OF 6, (`Dollars by area` OF 6100, 7625, 7625, 7625, 6100, 7014, 6100))
      , (`Table row` OF 7, (`Dollars by area` OF 6881, 8601, 8601, 8601, 6881, 7912, 6881))
      , (`Table row` OF 8, (`Dollars by area` OF 7662, 9577, 9577, 9577, 7662, 8810, 7662))

-- Each additional member above 8: a dollar amount PER PERSON, not a total for a household of 9 (s 2014(c) Table 3 gross monthly income limit where elderly or disabled members are a separate household, FY 2027).
`s 2014(c) Table 3 gross monthly income limit where elderly or disabled members are a separate household, FY 2027, each additional member` MEANS `Dollars by area` OF 781, 977, 977, 977, 781, 898, 781

-- One column of a `Dollars by area`, chosen by the place.
GIVEN d IS A `Dollars by area`
      area IS AN Area
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` MEANS
    CONSIDER area
        WHEN `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` THEN d's `in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia`
        WHEN `Alaska, urban` THEN d's `in Alaska, urban`
        WHEN `Alaska, rural 1` THEN d's `in Alaska, rural 1`
        WHEN `Alaska, rural 2` THEN d's `in Alaska, rural 2`
        WHEN Guam THEN d's `in Guam`
        WHEN Hawaii THEN d's `in Hawaii`
        WHEN `the Virgin Islands of the United States` THEN d's `in the Virgin Islands of the United States`

-- The row of a table for a household size: sizes 1 to 8 are rows; a household of 9 or more is the row for 8 plus the per-member figure for each member above 8.
-- The USDA states the per-member figure for each additional member; the Act does not say how a household above 8 is counted (NOTHING-kind: silent) -- a household below 1 member has no row.
GIVEN table IS AN `Annual table`
      increment IS A `Dollars by area`
      area IS AN Area
      size IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(c) the figure in the table for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF size LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a household of fewer than 1 member has no row
        IF size AT MOST 8
            THEN CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `household size` EQUALS size) (table's `the rows`)
                    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
                    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` (r's `the dollars`) area)
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `household size` EQUALS 8) (table's `the rows`)
                WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
                WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` (r's `the dollars`) area PLUS ((size MINUS 8) TIMES `s 2014(c) the figure for the area` increment area))

-- src:219 | The income standards of eligibility shall be adjusted each October 1 and shall provide that a household shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if—
-- src:220 | (1) the household’s income (after the exclusions and deductions provided for in subsections (d) and (e)) exceeds the poverty line, as defined in section 673(2) of the Community Services Block Grant Act (42 U.S.C. 9902(2)), for the forty-eight contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands of the United States, and Guam, respectively; and
@ref s 2014(c)(1), the poverty line (src:219-220)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      area IS AN Area
      size IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(c)(1) the poverty line for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fiscal year` EQUALS 2027
            THEN `s 2014(c) the figure in the table for the household` `s 2014(c)(1) Table 1 net monthly income limit, FY 2027` `s 2014(c)(1) Table 1 net monthly income limit, FY 2027, each additional member` area size
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): only the fiscal year 2027 figures were supplied; the poverty line is set outside this Act (section 673(2) of the Community Services Block Grant Act)

-- The limit is the USDA's published Table 2 figure (130 percent of the poverty level, in whole dollars), held as data like Table 1 and Table 3.
-- It is NOT 1.3 times the whole-dollar Table 1 figure: neither the Act (lines 219-222 of inputs/usc07-ch51.txt) nor the COLA page says how a percentage of the poverty line is rounded,
-- Table 2 is the only FY 2027 figure in the sources that is stated to be the gross monthly income limit, and 1.3 times the already-rounded Table 1 gives figures that appear in no source
-- (up to a dollar and a half from the published ones). The Act's own words, 30 per centum over a poverty line a caller supplies, stay in `s 2014(c)(2) the household is ineligible because its gross income exceeds the poverty line by more than 30 per centum`.
-- src:221 | in the case of a household that does not include an elderly or disabled member, the household’s income (after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)) exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum.
@ref s 2014(c)(2), the gross income test (src:221)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      area IS AN Area
      size IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(c)(2) the gross monthly income limit for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fiscal year` EQUALS 2027
            THEN `s 2014(c) the figure in the table for the household` `s 2014(c)(2) Table 2 gross monthly income limit, FY 2027` `s 2014(c)(2) Table 2 gross monthly income limit, FY 2027, each additional member` area size
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): only the fiscal year 2027 figures were supplied; the poverty line and its 30 per centum are set outside this Act's figures

-- src:220 | (1) the household’s income (after the exclusions and deductions provided for in subsections (d) and (e)) exceeds the poverty line, as defined in section 673(2) of the Community Services Block Grant Act (42 U.S.C. 9902(2)), for the forty-eight contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands of the United States, and Guam, respectively; and
-- src:221 | (2) in the case of a household that does not include an elderly or disabled member, the household’s income (after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)) exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum.
@ref s 2014(c), the standard for the 165 percent test of section 2012(m)(3) (src:220-221)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      area IS AN Area
      size IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(c) the USDA's Table 3 limit for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fiscal year` EQUALS 2027
            THEN `s 2014(c) the figure in the table for the household` `s 2014(c) Table 3 gross monthly income limit where elderly or disabled members are a separate household, FY 2027` `s 2014(c) Table 3 gross monthly income limit where elderly or disabled members are a separate household, FY 2027, each additional member` area size
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): only the fiscal year 2027 figures were supplied

-- src:219 | The income standards of eligibility shall be adjusted each October 1 and shall provide that a household shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if—
-- src:220 | (1) the household’s income (after the exclusions and deductions provided for in subsections (d) and (e)) exceeds the poverty line, as defined in section 673(2) of the Community Services Block Grant Act (42 U.S.C. 9902(2)), for the forty-eight contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands of the United States, and Guam, respectively; and
@ref s 2014(c)(1), net income (src:219-220)
GIVEN `the household's income after the exclusions and deductions provided for in subsections (d) and (e)` IS A NUMBER
      `the poverty line for the household` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(c)(1) the household is ineligible because its net income exceeds the poverty line` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household's income after the exclusions and deductions provided for in subsections (d) and (e)` GREATER THAN `the poverty line for the household`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a household shall be ineligible ... if ... the household's income ... exceeds the poverty line"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a household shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if" its income "exceeds the poverty line" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- The test against a limit in dollars (the published Table 2 figure, `s 2014(c)(2) the gross monthly income limit for the household`). The rule below it states the Act's own words over a poverty line.
-- src:221 | in the case of a household that does not include an elderly or disabled member, the household’s income (after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)) exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum.
@ref s 2014(c)(2), gross income against the limit in dollars (src:221)
GIVEN `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household's income after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)` IS A NUMBER
      `the gross monthly income limit for the household` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(c)(2) the household is ineligible because its gross income exceeds the gross monthly income limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the household's income after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)` GREATER THAN `the gross monthly income limit for the household`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a household shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if" its income "exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "if" clause is "(2) in the case of a household that does not include an elderly or disabled member, the household's income ... exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum"; a household that includes such a member fails that clause (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum" (the limit is the poverty line plus 30 per centum)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the household includes an elderly or disabled member was not supplied, and the income is over the limit

-- src:221 | in the case of a household that does not include an elderly or disabled member, the household’s income (after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)) exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum.
@ref s 2014(c)(2), gross income (src:221)
GIVEN `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household's income after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)` IS A NUMBER
      `the poverty line for the household` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(c)(2) the household is ineligible because its gross income exceeds the poverty line by more than 30 per centum` MEANS
    `s 2014(c)(2) the household is ineligible because its gross income exceeds the gross monthly income limit`
        `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
        `the household's income after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)`
        (`the poverty line for the household` TIMES 1.3)

-- src:219 | The income standards of eligibility shall be adjusted each October 1 and shall provide that a household shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if—
-- src:220 | (1) the household’s income (after the exclusions and deductions provided for in subsections (d) and (e)) exceeds the poverty line, as defined in section 673(2) of the Community Services Block Grant Act (42 U.S.C. 9902(2)), for the forty-eight contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands of the United States, and Guam, respectively; and
-- src:221 | (2) in the case of a household that does not include an elderly or disabled member, the household’s income (after the exclusions provided for in subsection (d) but before the deductions provided for in subsection (e)) exceeds such poverty line by more than 30 per centum.
@ref s 2014(c), the two standards together (src:219-221)
GIVEN `s 2014(c)(1) the net income test` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2014(c)(2) the gross income test` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(c) the household is ineligible on income` MEANS
    `snap1 either` `s 2014(c)(1) the net income test` `s 2014(c)(2) the gross income test`

-- src:222 | In no event shall the standards of eligibility for the Virgin Islands of the United States or Guam exceed those in the forty-eight contiguous States.
@ref s 2014(c), last sentence (src:222)
GIVEN `the standard of eligibility for Guam or the Virgin Islands` IS A NUMBER
      `the standard of eligibility in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(c) the standard of eligibility for Guam or the Virgin Islands after the cap` MEANS
    minimum (LIST `the standard of eligibility for Guam or the Virgin Islands`, `the standard of eligibility in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia`)

-- src:219 | The income standards of eligibility shall be adjusted each October 1 and shall provide that a household shall be ineligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if—
@ref s 2014(c), the adjustment date (src:219)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(c) the standards are adjusted on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF DATE_DAY day EQUALS 1 AND DATE_MONTH day EQUALS 10 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "adjusted each October 1" does not say that the standards may not change on another date
